* Range sequencer and over-current trip: the behavior that the specification
* asks of the programs of the controller (rules F-16, F-17 and F-18, section
* 4.4). No such program exists yet. This is a model of the rules, not of an
* implementation: it has no clock, and its reaction time is a parameter.
*
* Inputs, logic levels of the controller (vlogic):
*   cmp_up, cmp_jump, cmp_oc   the three comparators
*   down     a pulse asks for one step down (firmware); ignored while
*            cmp_up is high or a change is in progress
*   enable   low: range 0, every gate low
*   out_on   the request to close the output switch
* Outputs, same levels, behind the resistance of a pad (rpad):
*   g1 g2 g3   gates of the range switches, one-hot with overlap
*   a0 a1      address of the multiplexer
*   gout       gate of the output switch; low after a trip
* Rules:
*   F-16  cmp_jump forces range 3 after tseq, in every state, never blanked.
*   F-17  every change is make-before-break: the new gate and the address
*         change together, the old gate falls toverlap later; cmp_up is
*         ignored from the first change until tblank after the last one.
*   F-18  in range 3, cmp_oc high without interruption for toc opens the
*         output switch until the model is reset.
*
* The logic is written with products and sums of signals between 0 and 1,
* never with min, max or a comparison: those have corners, and the solver
* stops at a corner that lies where a signal rests. "a or b" is
* 1 - (1 - a)*(1 - b), "a and b" is a*b.
.func seq_hi(x) {0.5*(1 + tanh((x - 0.5)*20))}

* Set-reset latch on a 0 to 1 scale; reset wins.
.subckt SEQ_LATCH s r q
Cq q 0 5p
Rq q 0 1e12
Bq 0 q I = 1m*((1 - seq_hi(v(r)))*(seq_hi(v(s)) + (1 - seq_hi(v(s)))*seq_hi(v(q))) - v(q))
.ends SEQ_LATCH

.subckt SEQUENCER cmp_up cmp_jump cmp_oc down enable out_on g1 g2 g3 a0 a1 gout
+ params: vlogic=3.3 tseq=100n toverlap=1u tblank=2u toc=12u rpad=33
* inputs on a 0 to 1 scale, with the reaction time of the sequencer
Bup upr 0 V = seq_hi(v(cmp_up)/{vlogic})
Bju jur 0 V = seq_hi(v(cmp_jump)/{vlogic})
Boc ocr 0 V = seq_hi(v(cmp_oc)/{vlogic})
Bdn dnr 0 V = seq_hi(v(down)/{vlogic})
Ben en 0 V = seq_hi(v(enable)/{vlogic})
Bon on 0 V = seq_hi(v(out_on)/{vlogic})
Xdup upr ups DLY td={tseq}
Xdju jur jus DLY td={tseq}
Xddn dnr dns DLY td={tseq}
* the range as three latches: range 1 or more, 2 or more, 3
X1 s1 r1 l1 SEQ_LATCH
X2 s2 r2 l2 SEQ_LATCH
X3 s3 r3 l3 SEQ_LATCH
* Each latch has a copy delayed by the overlap and the blanking time. A step
* is taken only from a state that this copy confirms, so that a state must
* have stood for the whole blanking time before the next step, up or down.
* That is the blanking of rule F-17. A condition never names the latch it
* sets or clears: a latch that takes away its own drive on the way stops
* half way.
Xq1 l1 l1d DLY td={toverlap + tblank}
Xq2 l2 l2d DLY td={toverlap + tblank}
Xq3 l3 l3d DLY td={toverlap + tblank}
Bupok upok 0 V = v(ups)*v(en)
Bdnok dnok 0 V = v(dns)*(1 - v(ups))*v(en)
Bjump jump 0 V = v(jus)*v(en)
Bs1 s1 0 V = 1 - (1 - v(upok)*(1 - v(l1d)))*(1 - v(jump))
Bs2 s2 0 V = 1 - (1 - v(upok)*v(l1)*v(l1d)*(1 - v(l2d)))*(1 - v(jump))
Bs3 s3 0 V = 1 - (1 - v(upok)*v(l2)*v(l2d)*(1 - v(l3d)))*(1 - v(jump))
Br1 r1 0 V = 1 - (1 - v(dnok)*v(l1d)*(1 - v(l2))*(1 - v(l2d)))*v(en)
Br2 r2 0 V = 1 - (1 - v(dnok)*v(l2d)*(1 - v(l3))*(1 - v(l3d)))*v(en)
Br3 r3 0 V = 1 - (1 - v(dnok)*v(l3d))*v(en)
* one gate at a time, the old one held for the overlap
Bh1 h1 0 V = v(l1)*(1 - v(l2))
Bh2 h2 0 V = v(l2)*(1 - v(l3))
Bh3 h3 0 V = v(l3)
Xo1 h1 h1d DLY td={toverlap}
Xo2 h2 h2d DLY td={toverlap}
Xo3 h3 h3d DLY td={toverlap}
Bg1 g1i 0 V = {vlogic}*(1 - (1 - v(h1))*(1 - v(h1d)))
Bg2 g2i 0 V = {vlogic}*(1 - (1 - v(h2))*(1 - v(h2d)))
Bg3 g3i 0 V = {vlogic}*(1 - (1 - v(h3))*(1 - v(h3d)))
Ba0 a0i 0 V = {vlogic}*(v(h1) + v(h3))
Ba1 a1i 0 V = {vlogic}*v(l2)
Rg1 g1i g1 {rpad}
Rg2 g2i g2 {rpad}
Rg3 g3i g3 {rpad}
Ra0 a0i a0 {rpad}
Ra1 a1i a1 {rpad}
* over-current trip: a timer that runs while cmp_oc is high in range 3; it
* rises by 1 V per microsecond, stops near 40 V and falls back in nanoseconds
Ct tm 0 1p
Rt tm 0 1e12
Bgo go 0 V = seq_hi(v(ocr)*v(h3))
Bt 0 tm I = v(go)*1u*(1 - seq_hi((v(tm) - 39)/2)) - (1 - v(go))*1m*v(tm)
Bts ts 0 V = seq_hi(v(tm) - {toc*1e6} + 0.5)
Bzero zero 0 V = 1 - v(en)
Xtrip ts zero trip SEQ_LATCH
Bgo2 goi 0 V = {vlogic}*v(on)*v(en)*(1 - v(trip))
Rgo goi gout {rpad}
.ends SEQUENCER
